@startuml ComplexityComparison
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam bar {
    BackgroundColor #E3F2FD
    BorderColor #1565C0
}
skinparam rectangle {
    BackgroundColor #E3F2FD
    BorderColor #1565C0
}

title Algorithm Complexity Comparison — Cairo Network (V=35, E≈120)

package "Time Complexity (Operations)" {
    rectangle "BFS\nO(V+E)\n155 ops" as BFS
    rectangle "Dijkstra (heap)\nO((V+E)logV)\n896 ops" as DIJK
    rectangle "Dijkstra (array)\nO(V²)\n1,225 ops" as DIJK_ARR
    rectangle "A*\nO((V+E)logV)\n~448 ops" as ASTAR
    rectangle "Bellman-Ford\nO(VE)\n4,200 ops" as BF
    rectangle "Fibonacci Heap\nO(VlogV+E)\n610 ops" as FIB
    rectangle "Bidirectional\nO((V+E)logV)/2\n~448 ops" as BIDIR
}

note right of DIJK
  **Cairo Network Parameters:**
  V = 35 nodes
  E ≈ 120 edges
  Avg degree = 6.9
  
  Dijkstra (binary heap):
  - Enqueue: <= E times
  - Dequeue: <= V+E times
  - Each: O(log E) ~= O(log V)
  - Total: O((V+E) log V)
end note

note bottom of ASTAR
  **A* Average Case:**
  With admissible heuristic:
  explores ~50% fewer nodes
  
  Heuristic: h(n) = Euclidean
  Admissible: h(n) <= delta(n,t) [OK]
  Consistent: h(u) <= w(u,v) + h(v) [OK]
end note

note left of BF
  **Bellman-Ford:**
  Works with negative weights
  Detects negative cycles
  O(VE) = O(35 × 120) = 4,200
  
  4.7× slower than Dijkstra
  Unnecessary for road networks
end note

BFS --> DIJK
DIJK --> DIJK_ARR
DIJK_ARR --> ASTAR
ASTAR --> BF
BF --> FIB
FIB --> BIDIR

@enduml
